<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_PA-113.1-enterprise-architecture-framework-standards-and-governance" targetNamespace="https://erpplans.local/bpmn" exporter="erpplans generate-bpmn.py" exporterVersion="1.0">
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3569" name="W3569. Enterprise Architecture Strategy, Framework &amp; Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual IT/business strategy (links to VS-33); CIO/ExCo cycle
Frequency: Annual + on major change
Volume: Enterprise-wide
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / CIO
Participants: Chief Enterprise Architect, CIO, Business Capability Owners, IT Leadership (links to VS-27/VS-30/VS-99), Strategy (links to VS-33), PMO (links to VS-112), Security (links to VS-27.3), Data Office (links to VS-28.2)
Source: workflow W3569 — Enterprise Architecture Strategy, Framework &amp; Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3569_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3569_Lane1" name="Chief Enterprise Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3569_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3569_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3569_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3569_Lane2" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3569_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3569_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3569_Start4" name="Annual IT/business strategy (links to VS-33); CIO/ExCo cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3569_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3569_Task5" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/CIO define the EA strategy and framework: EA charter…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chief Enterprise Architect/CIO define the EA strategy and framework: EA charter and scope (business, data, application, technology, security architectures), the EA framework/method adoption (TOGAF or equivalent adapted), the link to business strategy and capability model (links to VS-33), and the governance operating model (board, authorities, cadence links to W3571)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / CIO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3569_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3569_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3569_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Leadership establish the EA function and governance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect/Leadership establish the EA function and governance: EA team and roles, the Architecture Review Board (ARB links to W3571), the principles/standards/reference-architecture program (W3570), the technology-standards/approved-list (W3572), and the integration to the PMO (links to VS-112/W3546) and IT operations (links to VS-27)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / IT Leadership
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3569_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3569_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3569_Task7" name="CIO/Chief Enterprise Architect ratify the EA strategy and governance with ExCo…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CIO/Chief Enterprise Architect ratify the EA strategy and governance with ExCo (links to VS-33/VS-36), secure the EA investment (links to VS-40/W3588), communicate the mandate to the organization, and report EA posture to the board (links to VS-36) and audit (links to VS-21)
Responsible (R): CIO / Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3569_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3569_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3569_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3569_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3569_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-144 (ensure architecture standards &amp; exception control.) | - operational: board-ratified charter and ARB authority (W3571); operational: pragmatic, capability-aligned scope
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3569_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3569_Annotation9" targetRef="W3569_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3569_Flow11" sourceRef="W3569_Start4" targetRef="W3569_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3569_Flow12" sourceRef="W3569_Task5" targetRef="W3569_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3569_Flow13" sourceRef="W3569_Task6" targetRef="W3569_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3569_Flow14" sourceRef="W3569_Task7" targetRef="W3569_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W3569_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W3569_plane" bpmnElement="W_W3569">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W3569_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W3569_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="950" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
