    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3570" name="W3570. Architecture Principles, Standards &amp; Reference Architecture" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: EA strategy (W3569); standards cycle; major change
Frequency: Maintained + annual refresh
Volume: Enterprise architecture layer
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect
Participants: Enterprise Architects (business/data/application/technology/security), Domain Architects, IT Leadership (links to VS-27/VS-28/VS-99), Security (links to VS-27.3), Data Office (links to VS-28.2)
Source: workflow W3570 — Architecture Principles, Standards &amp; Reference Architecture</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3570_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3570_Lane1" name="Enterprise Architects">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3570_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3570_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3570_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3570_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3570_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3570_Start3" name="EA strategy (W3569); standards cycle; major change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3570_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3570_Task4" name="Enterprise Architects define and maintain the architecture principles…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Enterprise Architects define and maintain the architecture principles: business-aligned principles (capability-driven, reuse-before-buy, standards-first, cloud-native, API-first, data-as-a-product, secure-by-design), and the decision rights/rationale for each; publish and socialize
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3570_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3570_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3570_Task5" name="Enterprise Architects/Domain Architects develop the reference architectures…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enterprise Architects/Domain Architects develop the reference architectures: business-capability map, application-reference patterns (ERP-centric, surrounding-application, integration patterns links to W3579), data-reference patterns (links to W3581), deployment/availability patterns (links to W3582), and security patterns (links to W3583); map to the BuildRight landscape (POS, ERP, ecommerce, loyalty, WMS, payments, BI)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects / Domain Architects
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3570_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3570_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3570_Task6" name="Enterprise Architects maintain the architecture standards catalog…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enterprise Architects maintain the architecture standards catalog: coding/design standards, integration standards (API/event/file), data standards (links to VS-29/VS-28.2), naming conventions, UI/UX standards (links to VS-10/VS-75), and documentation standards; publish to the repository (W3575) and enforce via ARB review (W3571)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3570_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3570_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3570_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3570_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3570_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-568 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Architecture Framework, Standards &amp; Governance (PA-113.1).) | - operational: annual refresh and ARB currency; operational: reference architectures and ARB enforcement
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3570_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3570_Annotation8" targetRef="W3570_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3570_Flow10" sourceRef="W3570_Start3" targetRef="W3570_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3570_Flow11" sourceRef="W3570_Task4" targetRef="W3570_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3570_Flow12" sourceRef="W3570_Task5" targetRef="W3570_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3570_Flow13" sourceRef="W3570_Task6" targetRef="W3570_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W3570_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W3570_plane" bpmnElement="W_W3570">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W3570_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W3570_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="950" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
