    <bpmn:process id="W_W3572" name="W3572. Technology Standards &amp; Approved Technology List" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: EA standards cycle (W3570); vendor/technology evaluation; end-of-life/refresh
Frequency: Maintained + quarterly update
Volume: Enterprise technology estate
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / Domain Architects
Participants: Domain Architects, IT Operations (links to VS-27.2), Security (links to VS-27.3), ITAM (links to VS-99), Procurement (links to VS-34), Innovation (links to VS-30), Vendor Management (links to VS-03)
Source: workflow W3572 — Technology Standards &amp; Approved Technology List</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3572_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3572_Lane1" name="Domain Architects">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3572_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3572_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3572_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3572_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3572_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3572_Start3" name="EA standards cycle (W3570); vendor/technology evaluation; end-of-life/refresh">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3572_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3572_Task4" name="Domain Architects/IT Operations maintain the technology standards and Approved…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Domain Architects/IT Operations maintain the technology standards and Approved Technology List (ATL): approved languages/frameworks, databases, middleware/integration platforms, cloud services, operating systems, hypervisors, observability tools, BI/analytics platforms, and retirement/eol technologies; classify as adopt/trial/assess/hold (radar model)
Responsible (R): Domain Architects / IT Ops
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3572_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3572_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3572_Task5" name="Domain Architects/Security/ITAM govern technology selection: approved…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Domain Architects/Security/ITAM govern technology selection: approved vendors/products, security review (links to VS-27.3), license/SAM implications (links to VS-99.2), supportability by IT operations (links to VS-27.1), total cost (links to W3588), and strategic fit (W3589); route exceptions to waiver (W3573)
Responsible (R): Domain Architects / Security / ITAM
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per selection</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3572_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3572_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3572_Task6" name="Domain Architects publish the ATL and standards to the repository (W3575)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Domain Architects publish the ATL and standards to the repository (W3575), integrate to procurement gatekeeping (links to VS-34 — non-ATL purchases require waiver) and to the PMO/solution-architecture review (W3571), and retire/deprecate technologies on a managed timeline (links to W3578)
Responsible (R): Domain Architects
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3572_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3572_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3572_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3572_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3572_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-144 (ensure architecture standards &amp; exception control.) | - operational: procurement gatekeeping and discovery; operational: radar model and quarterly update
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect / Domain Architects</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3572_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3572_Annotation8" targetRef="W3572_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
