    <bpmn:process id="W_W3573" name="W3573. Architecture Compliance, Exception &amp; Waiver Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Non-conformance detected; project request to deviate from standards
Frequency: Per request + continuous monitoring
Volume: Enterprise-wide
Owner: ARB / Chief Enterprise Architect
Participants: ARB, Enterprise Architects, Project/Solution Architects, PMO (links to VS-112), IT Operations (links to VS-27), Security (links to VS-27.3), Audit (links to VS-21)
Source: workflow W3573 — Architecture Compliance, Exception &amp; Waiver Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3573_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3573_Lane1" name="Solution Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3573_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3573_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3573_Lane2" name="ARB">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3573_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3573_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3573_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3573_Start4" name="Non-conformance detected; project request to deviate from standards">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3573_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3573_Task5" name="Project/Solution Architect raise an architecture exception/waiver request when…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project/Solution Architect raise an architecture exception/waiver request when a deviation from principles (W3570), standards (W3572), or approved solution architecture (W3571) is needed: rationale, scope, risk, mitigation, and expiry/review date; submit to ARB
Responsible (R): Solution Architect / Project
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3573_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3573_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3573_Task6" name="ARB assess the waiver: risk to integration (W3579), security (W3583)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: ARB assess the waiver: risk to integration (W3579), security (W3583), operations (links to VS-27.1), data (W3581), technical debt (links to W3578), and total cost (W3588); decision — grant (with conditions/expiry), defer, or deny; capture the decision and remediation plan
Responsible (R): ARB
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3573_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3573_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3573_Task7" name="ARB/Enterprise Architects maintain the waiver register and remediation roadmap…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: ARB/Enterprise Architects maintain the waiver register and remediation roadmap, monitor expiry/retirement, feed waivers to the technical-debt backlog (W3578) and audit (links to VS-21), and report waiver volume/risk to governance (W3592); trend waivers as a signal of standards fit
Responsible (R): ARB / Enterprise Architects
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3573_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3573_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3573_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3573_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3573_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-144 (ensure architecture standards &amp; exception control.) | - operational: expiry dates and remediation roadmap; operational: discovery and compliance monitoring
Owner: ARB / Chief Enterprise Architect</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3573_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3573_Annotation9" targetRef="W3573_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
