    <bpmn:process id="W_W3574" name="W3574. Architecture Capability, Skills &amp; Center of Excellence" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: EA strategy (W3569); capability gap; annual skills planning
Frequency: Annual + on gap
Volume: Architecture community
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect
Participants: Chief Enterprise Architect, Enterprise/Domain/Solution Architects, HR/L&amp;D (links to VS-19.3/VS-103), IT Leadership, CoE members
Source: workflow W3574 — Architecture Capability, Skills &amp; Center of Excellence</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3574_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3574_Lane1" name="Chief Enterprise Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3574_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3574_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3574_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3574_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3574_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3574_Start3" name="EA strategy (W3569); capability gap; annual skills planning">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3574_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3574_Task4" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/HR define the EA capability and roles…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chief Enterprise Architect/HR define the EA capability and roles: enterprise/domain/solution/business/data/security architects, role profiles, competencies (TOGAF, cloud, integration, data, security, retail-domain), and the staffing model (centralized vs. federated vs. hybrid)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / HR
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3574_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3574_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3574_Task5" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/L&amp;D run the architecture skills and development…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect/L&amp;D run the architecture skills and development program: competency assessment, training/certification plan (links to VS-19.3), the Architecture Center of Excellence (CoE) for patterns/reuse/coaching, and the architect community of practice
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual + ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3574_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3574_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3574_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect manage external architect services where needed…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chief Enterprise Architect manage external architect services where needed (consultants/contractors links to VS-34/VS-98), balance internal vs. external capacity, and integrate to workforce planning (links to VS-103) and recruitment (links to VS-19.1)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / HR
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3574_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3574_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3574_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3574_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3574_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-568 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Architecture Framework, Standards &amp; Governance (PA-113.1).) | - operational: development program and CoE; operational: community of practice and documentation (W3575)
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
