    <bpmn:process id="W_W3576" name="W3576. Architecture Maturity Assessment &amp; Continuous Improvement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual cycle; strategy refresh (W3569); audit (links to VS-21)
Frequency: Annual + on audit
Volume: EA function and landscape
Owner: Chief Enterprise Architect
Participants: Chief Enterprise Architect, Enterprise Architects, Audit (links to VS-21), IT Leadership, ExCo (links to VS-33), Innovation (links to VS-30)
Source: workflow W3576 — Architecture Maturity Assessment &amp; Continuous Improvement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3576_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3576_Lane1" name="Chief Enterprise Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3576_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3576_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3576_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3576_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3576_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3576_Start3" name="Annual cycle; strategy refresh (W3569); audit (links to VS-21)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3576_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3576_Task4" name="Chief Enterprise Architect/Audit assess EA maturity against a model (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chief Enterprise Architect/Audit assess EA maturity against a model (e.g., TOGAF ACM / CMMI-style): business alignment, standards conformance, portfolio rationalization (W3577), integration maturity (W3579), data architecture (W3581), security architecture (W3583), governance effectiveness (W3571), and value delivered (W3588)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect / Audit
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3576_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3576_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3576_Task5" name="Chief Enterprise Architect identify strengths, gaps, and the improvement…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Chief Enterprise Architect identify strengths, gaps, and the improvement roadmap: remediate waivers/technical debt (W3573/W3578), advance integration/data/security maturity, and align to the technology roadmap (W3585); prioritize and resource
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3576_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3576_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3576_Task6" name="Chief Enterprise Architect report EA maturity, improvement progress, and value…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chief Enterprise Architect report EA maturity, improvement progress, and value to ExCo (links to VS-33.2) and the board (links to VS-36), and feed learnings to strategy (W3569) and standards (W3570)
Responsible (R): Chief Enterprise Architect
Accountable (A): CIO / CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3576_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3576_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3576_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3576_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
