    <bpmn:process id="W_W5517" name="W5517. SEP Paved Road &amp; Engineering Standard Governance for Built Products" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New built-product service starting (golden-path bootstrap); ring expansion; security-gate result; quarterly QBR cycle
Frequency: Continuous + per release ring + quarterly reporting
Volume: 2 built products (OMO, TPS) × ~6–12 services each; 100% of new services start on the golden path minus ARB-recorded exceptions; every deploy rides the ring model (~weekly per squad)
Owner: Head of Engineering (SEP)
Participants: Head of Engineering, SEP DevEx engineers, AppSec engineer (dotted to SEC lead), QA automation lead, build SRE, OMO/TPS Tech Leads &amp; squad PMs, ARB (exception records — links to W3573), INFRA SRE (PRR co-owner), SEC GRC cell (Tier-1-touching changes), IAP (contract-first integration — links to W3579), DP (data contracts)
Source: workflow W5517 — SEP Paved Road &amp; Engineering Standard Governance for Built Products</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5517_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5517_Lane1" name="DevEx engineers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5517_Lane2" name="SEP QA-automation lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5517_Lane3" name="Squad engineers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5517_Lane4" name="SEP build SRE">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5517_Lane5" name="Head of Engineering">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5517_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5517_Start7" name="New built-product service starting (golden-path bootstrap); ring expansion; security-gate…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5517_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5517_Task8" name="DevEx bootstrap every new service from the SEP golden-path templates — repo…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DevEx bootstrap every new service from the SEP golden-path templates — repo layout, CI/CD, observability, IaC; any deviation requires an ARB-recorded exception (W3573), and paved-road adoption (100% minus recorded exceptions) is reported at QBR
Responsible (R): DevEx engineers / Squad Tech Lead
Accountable (A): Head of Engineering
Duration: 0.5–1 day/service bootstrap</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5517_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5517_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5517_Task9" name="SEP enforce the engineering standard: trunk-based development with feature…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SEP enforce the engineering standard: trunk-based development with feature flags (no long-lived branches); contract-first integration — every cross-product call is an IAP-published contract with consumer-driven contract tests, no direct database access (links to W3579); data contracts on every DP-published dataset
Responsible (R): SEP QA-automation lead / IAP / DP
Accountable (A): Head of Engineering
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5517_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5517_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5517_Task10" name="Squads deploy on the ring model — internal ring → canary stores/DCs → fleet —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Squads deploy on the ring model — internal ring → canary stores/DCs → fleet — with automated SLO-burn rollback gates, independent of the ERP monthly train; the AppSec engineer runs the security gates: SAST + dependency scan on every merge, DAST before each ring expansion, SBOM per release, secrets never in code — and can block a ring expansion
Responsible (R): Squad engineers / AppSec engineer
Accountable (A): Head of Engineering
Duration: Per deploy</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5517_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5517_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5517_Task11" name="SEP + INFRA run the production readiness review before the first fleet ring…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SEP + INFRA run the production readiness review before the first fleet ring: on-call runbook, SLOs, capacity model, DR posture — typhoon-season resilience is a launch criterion, not a follow-up
Responsible (R): SEP build SRE / INFRA SRE
Accountable (A): Head of Engineering
Duration: 8–16 hours/service</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5517_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5517_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5517_Task12" name="Head of Engineering report squad DORA targets at QBR — deployment frequency ≥…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Head of Engineering report squad DORA targets at QBR — deployment frequency ≥ weekly, change lead time &lt; 1 week, MTTR &lt; 4 hours, change-failure rate &lt; 15% — alongside product outcome KPIs; changes touching Tier-1 workflows carry Tier &amp; Control Board sign-off (links to W1409/W391)
Responsible (R): Head of Engineering / SEP
Accountable (A): CIO (QBR)
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5517_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5517_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5517_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5517_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5517_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-568 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Architecture Framework, Standards &amp; Governance (PA-113.1).) | - operational: 100% golden-path starts — deviations only via ARB-recorded exception (W3573) | - operational: security gates — SAST + dependency scan per merge, DAST before ring expansion, SBOM per release; AppSec block right | - operational: production readiness review (SEP + INFRA) before first fleet ring
Owner: Head of Engineering (SEP)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
