    <bpmn:process id="W_W5575" name="W5575. Customization Decision Record (CDR) Intake, Admissibility Gate &amp; ARB Approval" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A configuration-exhausted gap proposes an in-suite extension (EXT/PER/LOC/INT class); a new interface requiring a custom schema object; a fit-gap register row re-dispositioned away from the standard tier
Frequency: Per proposal (event-driven) at the ARB cycle; quarterly register report to the SIB
Volume: ~15–25 CDRs/year across the EXT/PER/LOC/INT classes against a standing extension budget of 10 EXT builds, 150 page-level personalizations and 120 custom schema objects
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (CDR gate lead)
Participants: Head of Enterprise Architecture, ARB (approves the CDR — links to W3571), Owning PO &amp; BPO, Application Manager (links to W132), ERP System Administrator (upgrade-safety opinion — links to W495), SEC lead (controls/PII pre-read), Finance Controller (accounting-adjacent extensions), SIB (quarterly register review), FinOps/TBM analyst (links to VS-135/W4100)
Source: workflow W5575 — Customization Decision Record (CDR) Intake, Admissibility Gate &amp; ARB Approval</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5575_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5575_Lane1" name="Owning PO &amp; BPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5575_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5575_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5575_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
