      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5575_Start5" name="A configuration-exhausted gap proposes an in-suite extension (EXT/PER/LOC/INT class); a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5575_Task6" name="Owning PO &amp; BPO raise the customization proposal once the in-suite ladder is…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Owning PO &amp; BPO raise the customization proposal once the in-suite ladder is exhausted: the gap statement, the affected workflows and control ids, and the documented standard/configuration/personalization attempts with the reason each was inadequate — a proposal without the exhausted-ladder evidence is returned, not assessed
Responsible (R): Owning PO &amp; BPO
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 4–6 hours/proposal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5575_Task7" name="Head of EA run the eight-gate admissibility assessment: gap is real and no…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Head of EA run the eight-gate admissibility assessment: gap is real and no build product is register-assigned to it (links to W5515); the extension is edge-clean with a defined input, output and trigger and does not fork a process; objects are registered in the custom application registry only; the design is upgrade-safe under online patching; every touched control of the 808-control register is named with its post-change evidence path; a named owning team accepts run cost, monitoring and re-attestation; a retirement trigger and plan exist; and three-year build-and-run cost is below the value of closing the gap
Responsible (R): Head of EA / Owning PO &amp; BPO
Accountable (A): ARB
Duration: 6–10 hours/CDR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5575_Task8" name="Head of EA test the proposal against the standing extension budget by class; a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Head of EA test the proposal against the standing extension budget by class; a proposal that would exceed a cap is admissible only with CIO sign-off and the paired retirement of another extension of the same class, booked as a commitment in the retirement backlog (links to W5577)
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 hours/CDR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5575_Task9" name="Owning PO author the Customization Decision Record — context with workflow ids…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Owning PO author the Customization Decision Record — context with workflow ids and gap statement, alternatives tried, design with objects and integration points, control mapping and evidence path, operations with owning team and runbook, retirement trigger and migration-out plan, and the sign-off block
Responsible (R): Owning PO &amp; BPO / Solution Architect
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 6–10 hours/CDR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5575_Task10" name="ARB decide at the architecture cycle — approve, approve with conditions, defer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: ARB decide at the architecture cycle — approve, approve with conditions, defer or deny; a denied proposal returns to the standard or configuration tier and a conditional approval carries its conditions into the delivery change record (links to W132/W1409); the architecture opinion is recorded against the repository (links to W3575)
Responsible (R): ARB
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 1 hour/CDR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5575_Task11" name="Head of EA open the register entry for the approved record and report the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Head of EA open the register entry for the approved record and report the quarter&#x27;s CDR decisions, budget consumption by class and cycle-time performance to the SIB; denied and deferred proposals are reported with the ladder tier they returned to, so the gate&#x27;s own conversion rate stays visible
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5575_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5575_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5575_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5575_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-568 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Architecture Framework, Standards &amp; Governance (PA-113.1).) | - operational: no extension without an approved Customization Decision Record naming its controls, owner and retirement trigger | - operational: extension budget enforced by class — exceeding a cap requires CIO sign-off and a paired retirement commitment | - operational: product-modifying changes are inadmissible — the gate may approve extension, personalization, localization and interface classes only
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (CDR gate lead)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5575_Assoc14" sourceRef="W5575_Annotation13" targetRef="W5575_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
