    <bpmn:process id="W_W5576" name="W5576. CEMLI Register Maintenance &amp; Quarterly Object-Inventory Audit" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly register audit cycle; a completed patch rehearsal; an object discovered in the custom schema with no register row
Frequency: Quarterly audit; per-rehearsal verification; continuous on object discovery
Volume: The full non-configuration inventory — extension, personalization, localization-pack and interface rows with their schema objects, programs, templates and personalization paths — re-verified across 4 audits and ~5 patch rehearsals a year
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (customization register custodian)
Participants: Head of Enterprise Architecture, ERP System Administrator (object-inventory diff — links to W495), Application Manager (links to W132), Owning Team IT PO (per-row re-attestation), IT Security (links to W367), Internal Audit (links to VS-21/W387), SIB (quarterly review)
Source: workflow W5576 — CEMLI Register Maintenance &amp; Quarterly Object-Inventory Audit</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5576_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5576_Lane1" name="ERP System Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5576_Lane2" name="Head of EA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5576_Lane3" name="Owning Team IT PO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5576_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5576_Start5" name="Quarterly register audit cycle; a completed patch rehearsal; an object discovered in the…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5576_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5576_Task6" name="ERP System Administrator extract the current object inventory from the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: ERP System Administrator extract the current object inventory from the production and patch environments (links to W384) and diff it against the register&#x27;s declared objects, programs, templates and personalization paths
Responsible (R): ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 6–10 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5576_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5576_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5576_Task7" name="Head of EA adjudicate every diff line in both directions: an object present in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Head of EA adjudicate every diff line in both directions: an object present in the estate with no register row is raised as an incident rather than logged as a finding and routed to the gate for retrospective record or removal (links to W5575); a register row whose objects no longer exist is closed as retired and its budget reclaimed (links to W5577)
Responsible (R): Head of EA / Application Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per diff line</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5576_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5576_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5576_Task8" name="Owning Team IT PO re-attest each active row: the runbook is current, monitoring…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Owning Team IT PO re-attest each active row: the runbook is current, monitoring is in place, the named controls and their evidence paths still hold, and the retirement trigger is still the right one; an unattested row escalates to the owning team&#x27;s leadership at the next cycle
Responsible (R): Owning Team IT PO
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 0.5 hours/row</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5576_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5576_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5576_Task9" name="Head of EA verify that the patch rehearsal applied the register&#x27;s full…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Head of EA verify that the patch rehearsal applied the register&#x27;s full inventory and record the rehearsal that last proved each row; a row unproven by any rehearsal in the current cycle blocks the production patch until it is rehearsed or retired (links to W495)
Responsible (R): Head of EA / ERP System Administrator
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4–8 hours/rehearsal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5576_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5576_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5576_Task10" name="Head of EA report the audit to the SIB with the exception count, the incident…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Head of EA report the audit to the SIB with the exception count, the incident register for unregistered objects, per-class budget consumption and rehearsal coverage; unresolved exceptions carry into the next cycle with a named remediation owner and date
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5576_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5576_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5576_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5576_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5576_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-568 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Architecture Framework, Standards &amp; Governance (PA-113.1).) | - operational: an object in the custom schema with no register row is an incident, not an audit finding | - operational: quarterly per-row owner re-attestation covering runbook, monitoring, controls and retirement trigger | - operational: production patching is blocked until the register&#x27;s full inventory has been rehearsed in the patch environment
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (customization register custodian)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
