    <bpmn:process id="W_W5577" name="W5577. Extension De-Customization, Retirement &amp; Budget Reclamation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A vendor release ships equivalent standard function; a register row&#x27;s usage falls below threshold for two consecutive quarters; a process-mining finding shows the forked path costs more than the gap; a Philippine statute or format change supersedes a localization component; a module re-tiering re-scopes the in-suite footprint
Frequency: Trigger-driven; retirement review at the quarterly business review; standing target of at least one completion per half-year
Volume: ~6–10 fired retirement triggers/year against the standing inventory, converting to ~2 completed retirements/year at the steady-state extension budget
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (retirement backlog owner)
Participants: Head of Enterprise Architecture, Owning PO &amp; BPO (retirement execution), ARB (initiates retirement on a process-mining finding — links to W3571), Application Manager (links to W132), ERP System Administrator (links to W495), Finance Controller (accounting-adjacent rows), SIB (quarterly review), Internal Audit (links to VS-21)
Source: workflow W5577 — Extension De-Customization, Retirement &amp; Budget Reclamation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5577_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5577_Lane1" name="Head of EA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5577_Lane2" name="Owning PO &amp; BPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5577_Lane3" name="Owning Team IT PO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5577_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5577_Start5" name="A vendor release ships equivalent standard function; a register row&#x27;s usage falls below…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5577_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5577_Task6" name="Head of EA monitor the register&#x27;s retirement triggers against vendor release…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Head of EA monitor the register&#x27;s retirement triggers against vendor release content, usage telemetry, process-mining findings (links to W3577/W3592), Philippine regulatory change and in-suite footprint decisions (links to W5515); a fired trigger opens a retirement assessment rather than a discussion
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5577_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5577_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5577_Task7" name="Owning PO &amp; BPO assess the fired trigger: does the standard function reach…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Owning PO &amp; BPO assess the fired trigger: does the standard function reach parity on the workflows and controls the extension carries, what data migrates out, which interfaces and reports depend on the objects, and what the cutover window costs; the assessment ends in a retirement plan with a date or a documented reason the trigger does not apply this cycle
Responsible (R): Owning PO &amp; BPO
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 4–8 hours/trigger</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5577_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5577_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5577_Task8" name="Head of EA set the retirement clock on a parity trigger — the owning team has…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Head of EA set the retirement clock on a parity trigger — the owning team has two quarters to adopt the standard function and retire the extension; a slip is escalated to the SIB with the run cost the estate keeps paying, not renegotiated silently
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per fired trigger</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5577_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5577_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5577_Task9" name="Owning Team IT PO execute the retirement through the standard delivery rails…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Owning Team IT PO execute the retirement through the standard delivery rails (links to W132/W1409): migrate data out, re-point dependent interfaces and reports, re-map the affected controls to their standard-function evidence path, drop the objects, and confirm the drop in the next environment diff (links to W5576)
Responsible (R): Owning Team IT PO / Application Manager
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 24–60 hours/extension</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5577_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5577_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5577_Task10" name="Head of EA close the register row as retired, reclaim its budget slot by class…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Head of EA close the register row as retired, reclaim its budget slot by class, release any paired-retirement commitment the gate booked against it (links to W5575), and report the completion at the quarterly review with the run cost and patch-merge effort the estate stopped carrying
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5577_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5577_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5577_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5577_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5577_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-568 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Architecture Framework, Standards &amp; Governance (PA-113.1).) | - operational: every register row carries a retirement trigger; a row without one cannot be approved at the gate | - operational: a parity trigger starts a two-quarter retirement clock, and a slip is escalated to the SIB with its carried run cost | - operational: a row is closed only after the environment diff confirms its objects are gone and its controls are re-mapped
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture (retirement backlog owner)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
